  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "e5UYDwTUfRdieOwZuIZ/g1QRWzs=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:10.704Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Softwire is a London bespoke development shop that the assessment reads as the right size with a modern stack. Bespoke delivery means no proprietary platform to protect, and size is the axis on which most leads in this set fail \u2014 several otherwise strong candidates are held back purely for being too large.\n\nThe open-source posture is unverified and the stack was not researched in detail, so the screen is incomplete rather than negative. As with the other right-size UK leads, that screen is the only work standing between the current priority-3 placement and a decision either way.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- Softwire (UK \u00b7 not verified)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> London bespoke shop, right size, modern stack. OSS posture unverified.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:29:10.704880Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:10.704885Z"
    }
  },
